\mouse returns the position of the mouse inside the
LiveLily window, in pixels, as two values, x and y.
It takes no arguments. To see its value, call it with
\print:

\print \mouse

It can also be used as an argument to other commands,
like send of an OSC client, which will send two integers:

\myosc.send "/mouse" \mouse

To get only one of the two values, use \mousex or \mousey.
